{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs as main carries it, at merge commit e677dd8f54f1380040e19a36a290f7a32f7841d5, which landed the reviewed-paths work approved by codex in 66e46023 and ratified in 4c64bd4d.\n\nThe merge changed docs/reference/architecture.md, docs/reference/gs/merge.md and docs/reference/gs/review.md, bringing the pages into line with a merge that may reach every path its approval reviewed.\n\nThis replaces f6dc6052, published by gs merge for this same commit and stale from birth; the cause is recorded in the accompanying assert.\n\nOne consequence belongs on the docs artifact, because documentation is what feels it. This run retired 7463de51, cited by twelve pages, and 0d7b8dde, cited by eleven. Under the previous rule both retirements were refused outright, which is why those pages carried stale anchors for days with no legal way out — the successor cannot exist until the merge lands, and the merge could not land until the pages were repointed. Retired with a covering successor, they now flare: the gate follows the supersession to the current pointer and reports the pages as out of date rather than failing the set. Those pages should be re-anchored, and that is ordinary work with its own request, not a blocker.\n\nIt rests on 9891ec40 at internal/gitstore, live and not stale, at a path this merge does not touch.","body":{"commit":"e677dd8f54f1380040e19a36a290f7a32f7841d5","path":"docs"}}